  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Fractions of amounts"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I find a fraction of an amount?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Method 1**\n**Divide** by the **denominator** and **multiply** by the **numerator**\n\n  - To find $\\frac{1}{3}$ of $90$, divide it by 3\n  \n    - $90\\div3=30$\n  - To find $\\frac{2}{5}$ of $60$, divide it by 5 then multiply it by 2\n  \n    - $60\\div5=12$, then $12\\times2=24$\n- **Method 2**\nChange the fraction into a **decimal**, then **multiply**\n\n  - To find $\\frac{1}{4}$ of $16$, turn $\\frac{1}{4}$ into $0.25$ then multiply\n  \n    - $0.25\\times16=4$\n  - To find $\\frac{9}{10}$ of $15$, turn $\\frac{9}{10}$ into $0.9$ then multiply\n  \n    - $0.9\\times15=13.5$\n- **Method 3**\nWrite both numbers as fractions and **multiply two fractions** together\n\n  - To find $\\frac{2}{3}$ of $60$, write $60$ as $\\frac{60}{1}$\n  \n    - work out $\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{60}{1}=\\frac{120}{3}=40$\n  - To find $\\frac{5}{6}$ of $\\frac{8}{3}$\n  \n    - work out $\\frac{5}{6}\\times\\frac{8}{3}=\\frac{40}{18}=\\frac{20}{9}$"
  }
 ]
